{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1515586-victoria-era-wod","id":1515586,"title":"Victoria era WOD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-19T16:51:05-07:00","id":1515586,"title":"Victoria era WOD","content":"Hi folks I'm wondering since Mage Victorian Age is going to released, what about the other WOD books set in Victorian era such as Vampire and Werewolf the Wild West, the only ones that didn't get the 19th century treatment is Changeling and Wraith.<br /> <br /> LW","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3380-martian1912","name":"Martian1912","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-19T17:03:34-07:00","id":1515588,"title":"","content":"You probably aren't likely to see anything official, but there would certainly be a place for it in the Storytellers Vault.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T02:49:14-07:00","id":1515637,"title":"","content":"I will add that there is a lot of potential late 19th century story hooks for the two games to be found in places like Great Britain, Ireland, Germany, Italy, Egypt, New York, Chicago, New Orleans, San Francisco, Mexico, Cuba, Hawaii, Japan, and Hong Kong, among others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T14:22:20-07:00","id":1519664,"title":"","content":"There really is a lot of potential in more Victorian Age settings in general.<br /> <br /> I'm really interested in seeing the Storytellers Vault do Victorian Age versions of Changeling and Wraith. A lot of the modern pop culture takes on faeries originated in the Victorian era and the era was also a time of renewed interest in spiritualism and a fascination with death on both sides of the Atlantic.<br /> <br /> Come to think of it, I always wondered what the setting for the planned historical prequel game for Changeling in the 90's would've originally been.<br /> <br /> I know Vampire got Dark Ages (and that later got turned into a whole line of its own in Revised), Werewolf got the Wild West, Mage got the Renaissance with The Sorcerer's Crusade, and Wraith got World War I. I'm genuinely curious what Changeling's original historical prequel would've been.<br /> <br /> I do remember writing up a concept for a &quot;historical prequel&quot; for the Street Fighter RPG set in Ancient Rome and focused on gladiators in the arenas and Shadaloo being a mystery death cult trying to destroy the Roman Empire from within.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 08-03-2023, 05:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T00:08:06-07:00","id":1519713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1515586-victoria-era-wod?p=1519664#post1519664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know Vampire got Dark Ages (and that later got turned into a whole line of its own in Revised), Werewolf got the Wild West, Mage got the Renaissance with The Sorcerer's Crusade, and Wraith got World War I. I'm genuinely curious what Changeling's original historical prequel would've been.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically speaking all major splats but Wraith have their Dark Ages version. But afaik Dark Ages: Fae is totally different then Changeling: the Dreaming. And all but Vampire have only core books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T03:07:30-07:00","id":1519723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1515586-victoria-era-wod?p=1519664#post1519664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There really is a lot of potential in more Victorian Age settings in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>Our group has always preferred Victorian Age settings, the only game we hadn't played the era was WOD which we started up a year ago, of course if you want some of the modern nights background there is a degree of retconning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1515586-victoria-era-wod?p=1519664#post1519664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm really interested in seeing the Storytellers Vault do Victorian Age versions of Changeling and Wraith. A lot of the modern pop culture takes on faeries originated in the Victorian era and the era was also a time of renewed interest in spiritualism and a fascination with death on both sides of the Atlantic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well one of the MVA authors published a companion (material that didnt make the main book), from what I've seen the Changeling and Wraith Authors are writing era neutral or modern nights material, but here's hoping.<br /> <br /> I agree though these were the high eras for both settings as you've said Spiritualism and Mediumship were at their heights particularly with the mortality rates in industrialised society and the sheer levels of violence on the frontiers.<br /> Its also a time of great change for Changelings - Georgian times saw some good times with the rise of Romanticism, widescale publication and art, but Victorian times saw a definitive rise in Banality.<br /> <br /> Without derailing the thread this is our setting where essentially most of the WOD is in a state of quiet war for one reason or another, the overarching thread being the Stormeaters growth, WTA Tales from the Trails Mexico already features the Stormeater affecting the Dark Umbra and Wraiths.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1515586-victoria-era-wod?p=1519664#post1519664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Come to think of it, I always wondered what the setting for the planned historical prequel game for Changeling in the 90's would've originally been.<br /> <br /> I know Vampire got Dark Ages (and that later got turned into a whole line of its own in Revised), Werewolf got the Wild West, Mage got the Renaissance with The Sorcerer's Crusade, and Wraith got World War I. I'm genuinely curious what Changeling's original historical prequel would've been.</div> </div> </div> </div>We might never know, generally the lines need a signficant event to hinge around (which is why Dark Ages Mage falls a little flat as it lacks VDAs Princes War/Inquistion or DAFs decline of magic), and given the historical setting for CTL is the Victorian Era there's a high probablity it would have been, the challenge with doing Changeling the 60s or the Resurgence is IMHO it wouldn't have been that greatly different from the modern, although the return of the Sidhe is a flash point.<br /> <br /> I think the Victorian era has more meat for both settings as above the rise of Banality challenging the courts and how their efforts to counter this broke through the mists on a large number of occasions, plus the whole war between the Dark Kingdoms of Iron and Flint for Wraith, plus large swaithes of the British Shadowlands being besieged by Spectres (just look at the mortality rates in the Rookerys).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T06:52:09-07:00","id":1519741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1515586-victoria-era-wod?p=1519713#post1519713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Technically speaking all major splats but Wraith have their Dark Ages version. But afaik Dark Ages: Fae is totally different then Changeling: the Dreaming. And all but Vampire have only core books.</div> </div> </div> </div>True but that was during Revised and while Fae was totally different from Changeling, it was also kind of a historical prequel.<br /> <br /> During 2e, only Vampire had Dark Ages and it was part of a plan for the main five gamelines to have their own unique historical prequel. Werewolf had Wild West, Mage had the Renaissance, and Wraith had World War I but Changeling's prequel was never released.<br /> <br /> I always kinda pondered about some concepts for historical prequels for the later gamelines as well as for stuff like Street Fighter and the fan games such as Senshi: The Merchandising and Zombie: The Coil. These were my concepts...<br /> <br /> Hunter: The Revolutionary Age (1790's)<br /> Mummy: The Jazz Age (1920's)<br /> Changeling: The Victorian Age (1870's)<br /> Demon: The Baroque Age (1660's)<br /> Street Fighter: The Gladiator Age (Ancient Rome)<br /> Senshi: The Bubblegum Age (1970's)<br /> Zombie: The Brothers' War (American Civil War)<br /> <br /> Demon: The Baroque Age would probably be a lot closer to DA: Fae or Devil's Due than it would be to the modern Demon: The Fallen, while Hunter: The Revolutionary Age would be sort of like Dark Ages: Inquisitor where it's halfway between Reckoning and Hunters Hunted.<br /> <br /> Senshi's historical prequel would be unique because mechanically, it'd be mostly the same but the Cliques would be different, based on a mix of 60's and 70's anime and manga as well as American comics and movies. So you'd have the cliques based on stuff like Cutie Honey, the OG Devilman, Black Jack, Astro Boy, Speed Racer, Star Wars, The X-Men, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 08-04-2023, 09:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T15:56:49-07:00","id":1519798,"title":"","content":"Apologies for the double post, but I'm gonna have to repost this after my original post accidentally got flagged as spam when I tried to edit it. The mods can delete the original post if they want to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1515586-victoria-era-wod?p=1519713#post1519713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Technically speaking all major splats but Wraith have their Dark Ages version. But afaik Dark Ages: Fae is totally different then Changeling: the Dreaming. And all but Vampire have only core books.</div> </div> </div> </div>True but that was during Revised and while Fae was totally different from Changeling, it was also kind of a historical prequel.<br /> <br /> During 2e, only Vampire had Dark Ages and it was part of a plan for the main five gamelines to have their own unique historical prequel. Werewolf had Wild West, Mage had the Renaissance, and Wraith had World War I but Changeling's prequel was never released.<br /> <br /> I always kinda pondered about some concepts for historical prequels for the later gamelines as well as for stuff like Street Fighter and the fan games such as Senshi: The Merchandising and Zombie: The Coil. These were my concepts...<br /> <br /> Hunter: The Revolutionary Age (1790's)<br /> Mummy: The Jazz Age (1920's)<br /> Changeling: The Victorian Age (1870's)<br /> Demon: The Baroque Age (1660's)<br /> Street Fighter: The Gladiator Age (Ancient Rome)<br /> Senshi: The Bubblegum Age (1970's)<br /> Zombie: The Brothers' War (American Civil War)<br /> <br /> Demon: The Baroque Age would probably be a lot closer to DA: Fae or Devil's Due than it would be to the modern Demon: The Fallen, while Hunter: The Revolutionary Age would be sort of like Dark Ages: Inquisitor where it's halfway between Reckoning and Hunters Hunted.<br /> <br /> Senshi's historical prequel would be unique because mechanically, it'd be mostly the same but the Cliques would be different, based on a mix of 60's and 70's anime and manga as well as American comics and movies.<br /> <br /> So instead of cliques based on 90's anime like Sailor Moon and Magic Knight Rayearth, you'd have the cliques based on stuff like Cutie Honey, the OG Devilman, Black Jack, Astro Boy, Speed Racer, Star Wars, The X-Men, etc.<br /> <br /> I don't know anything about Gargoyles: The Vigil and I'm not sure what historical period could work for the old fan game based on Highlander.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-04T17:32:24-07:00","id":1519810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1515586-victoria-era-wod?p=1519713#post1519713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Technically speaking all major splats but Wraith have their Dark Ages version. But afaik Dark Ages: Fae is totally different then Changeling: the Dreaming. And all but Vampire have only core books.</div> </div> </div> </div>DA: Mage has Grimoire. A Brilliant, brilliant sourcebook and key expansion to the whole game. Inquisitor had a Companion, no idea about that one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":