ion that one was more of a supplement than a full gameline core book though, sort of like Blood &amp; Silk that tied VTDA to Kindred of the East and all the other Year Of The Lotus material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T11:08:46-07:00","id":1519887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1515586-victoria-era-wod?p=1519664#post1519664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm genuinely curious what Changeling's original historical prequel would've been.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the theories back in the day, based on how much space it got in the Changeling Storytellers Handbook, was the age of piracy in the Caribbean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-05T12:48:23-07:00","id":1519894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1515586-victoria-era-wod?p=1519887#post1519887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One of the theories back in the day, based on how much space it got in the Changeling Storytellers Handbook, was the age of piracy in the Caribbean.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not gonna lie, that would've been amazing to see.<br /> <br /> What did you think of my brief concepts for historical prequels for the minor WoD lines and unofficial fan games that I mentioned earlier?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T08:07:53-07:00","id":1519953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1515586-victoria-era-wod?p=1519894#post1519894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What did you think of my brief concepts for historical prequels for the minor WoD lines and unofficial fan games that I mentioned earlier?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm totally unfamiliar with the fan games, so I can't really say anything about them. <br /> <br /> I think there's a lot you can do with the Revolutionary Era (and by that, I mean the period between the Seven Years War/French &amp; Indian War and the battle of Waterloo). Adam Tinsworth, who did a lot of writing for Hunter, Demon, and Werewolf, once told me he had really wanted to do a Victorian Age Hunter book that would've focused on Hunters Hunted style characters who emulated the likes of Abraham Van Helsing and Sherlock Holmes, and I think that sort of thing can also work really well in the late 18th and very early 19th century. The 2001 film <i>Brotherhood of the Wolf</i> is a really great example of Hunters in that time period, with two veterans of the French &amp; Indian War investigating the Beast of G\u00e9vaudan. Also Tim Burton's 1999 film <i>Sleepy Hollow</i>, with Johnny Depp (before heavy drinking turned him into a parody of himself) playing Ichabod Craine as an early forensic scientists. (There's also Terry Gilliam's <i>The Brothers Grimm</i> from 2005, which is perhaps a little too humorous, but still has a lot of interesting ideas.) This is also the period when Mary Shelly's novel Frankenstein is set, as well as works by other early Gothic writers like Anne Radcliffe, Sophia Lee, and the so-called Graveyard poets. And you can draw on things like Dennis Wheatley's Roger Brook novels, Bernard Cornwall's Richard Sharpe novels, and Robert Lee Hall's mystery novels featuring Ben Franklin during his time in England. <br /> <br /> The 1920s is, effectively, part of the Wraith: The Great War setting, with the mortal war simply being the catalyst which leads to a near decade of upheaval in the lands of the dead. Humans who die during the early part of the Roaring 20s, the Jazz Age, Harlem Renaissance, Irish civil war, Ann\u00e9es Folles, Weimar Germany, the Polish-Soviet War, the Russian civil war, the Soviet Famine, the break up of the Ottoman Empire, the Japanese colonization of Korea, US occupation of Hispaniola and Nicaragua, the Patagonia uprising, and other events are going to find themselves thrown into the events of the Stygian civil war and the Great Maelstrom. But, obviously, there's a lot going on in the living world to play around with. It's the start of Hollywood, which I think has a lot of potential for a Changeling setting. <br /> <br /> The Baroque period has a lot to play with as well. Especially the time of the Sun King, Peter the Great, Carolus Rex, William and Mary, and Carlos II. If you've never seen it, Guy Davis (who did a lot of art for Vampire: The Masquerade during the Revised era) did a comic series called <i>The Marquis</i>, that is about a demon hunter battling demons in a fictional setting that is heavily based on early 18th century France, with a lot of Baroque influence in the architecture and clothing. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T08:52:17-07:00","id":1519957,"title":"","content":"Tangentially related, my old <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1381358-ages-of-darkness#post1381358\">Ages of Darkness thread</a>. (At some point I hope to go back and expand on a lot of them.)<br /> <br /> Savage Sands (Werewolf &amp; Mummy in @4th millenium BC/Antediluvian Egypt)<br /> The New City (Vampire &amp; Demon in Carthage, 550 - 340 BC)<br /> The Last Pharaohs (Vampire &amp; Mummy in Ptolemaic Egypt, 305 - 30 BC)<br /> Kingdoms of the Jaguar (Werewolf &amp; Mage in Classical Maya, 300 - 500 AD)<br /> The House of Wisdom (Vampire &amp; Mage in medieval Baghdad, 750 - 1258 AD)<br /> The First Renaissance (Vampire &amp; Mage in the Kingdom of the Franks, 760 - 840)<br /> Lords of the North (Werewolf &amp; Mage in medieval Scandinavia, 800 - 1000)<br /> Rodina (Mage &amp; Fae in Kievan Rus, 950 - 1100)<br /> The Edge of the World (Werewolf &amp; Mage in Vineland, 1000 - 1100)<br /> A Bloody Savage Conquest (Werewolf &amp; Wraith in Norman England, 1066 - 1076)<br /> The Dragon's Reign (Vampire &amp; Werewolf in Walachia, 1430 - 1477)<br /> Low Conquers High (Kindred of the East &amp; the Beast Courts in Sengoku Japan, 1467 - 1615)<br /> The Golden Century (Vampire &amp; Mage in Imperial Spain, 1492 - 1618)<br /> Bohemian Rhapsody (Mage &amp; Changeling in Prague, 1583 - 1611)<br /> In the Shadow of the Sun King (Vampire &amp; Changeling in France, 1643 - 1715)<br /> On Stranger Tides (Mage &amp; Changeling in the Caribbean, 1696 - 1725)<br /> Dark Satanic Mills (Werewolf &amp; Demon in Industrial Revolution England, 1770 - 1820)<br /> A Little Night Music (Wraith &amp; Changeling in Vienna, 1781 - 1791)<br /> Sleepy Hollows (Hunters Hunted &amp; Sorcerer in New York's Hudson River Valley, 1790 - 1820)<br /> Lost Kingdom (Mage &amp; Changeling in the Kingdom of Hawaii, 1793 - 1893)<br /> The Seminole Wars (Werewolf &amp; Mage in Florida, 1816 - 1858)<br /> The Rising Sun (The Beast Courts &amp; Mage in Meiji Japan, 1868 - 1912)<br /> Up From the Ashes (Vampire &amp; Wraith in Chicago, 1871 - 1881)<br /> Dreams of the White City (Mage &amp; Changeling a the Chicago Exhibition, 1893)<br /> Dreaming in the Darkness (Wraith &amp; Changeling in Lovecraft's Rhode Island, 1900 - 1938)<br /> Blood &amp; Fire (Vampire &amp; Werewolf in Mexico, 1910 - 1920)<br /> I Walk These Hills (Mage &amp; Twilight Folk in Appalachia, 1910 - 1940)<br /> Beautiful Wicked Pearl (Vampire &amp; Kindred of the East in Shanghai, 1917 - 1937)<br /> Dark Cabaret (Vampire &amp; Mage in Weimar Germany, 1918 - 1929)<br /> Harlem Nights (Vampire &amp; Mafia in New York City's Harlem, 1918 - 1938)<br /> The Chicago Way (Vampire &amp; Werewolf in Chicago, 1920 - 1931)<br /> Dark Skies (Project: Twilight &amp; The Technocracy in the American West, 1945 - 1970)<br /> In the Valley of Shadow (Vampire &amp; Wraith in LA, 1945 - 1960)<br /> Mascaras (Hunters Hunted &amp; Mummy in Mexico, 1955 - 1970)<br /> The Baron's Shadow (Vampire &amp; Wraith in Haiti, 1957 - 1971)<br /> California Dreamin' (Mage &amp; Changeling in Southern California, 1960 - 1970)<br /> Sunset People (Pariahs &amp; Twilight Folk in LA, 1972 - 1984)<br /> Rust Never Sleeps (Werewolf &amp; Changeling in the American Midwest, 1974 - 1984)<br /> Veterans of the Psychic Wars (Psychics &amp; Project: Twilight in the American Underground, 1974 - 1984)<br /> Cocaine Cowboys (Vampire &amp; Mafia in Miami, 1976 - 1992)<br /> Waiting for the Hammer to Fall (Vampire &amp; Wraith in the USSR, 1981 - 1991)<br /> Heroic Bloodshed (Kindred of the East &amp; The Beast Courts in Hong Kong, 1982 - 1996)<br /> End of Days (Hunter &amp; Demon in an alternate LA, 1999)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T08:54:12-07:00","id":1519960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1515586-victoria-era-wod?p=1519953#post1519953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> IAdam Tinsworth, who did a lot of writing for Hunter, Demon, and Werewolf, once told me he had really wanted to do a Victorian Age Hunter book that would've focused on Hunters Hunted style characters who emulated the likes of Abraham Van Helsing and Sherlock Holmes, and I think that sort of thing can also work really well in the late 18th and very early 19th century.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yes. I would indeed have loved to do that. It would have been thematically similar to H:tR, taking the idea of individuals thrust into a war they didn\u2019t understand without support or knowledge, but without the Solar Exalted Lite powers of the Imbued. It was probably back when I was working on London by Night, and thinking how this setting would work for Hunters. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27267-adders","name":"adders","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27267_1.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T07:41:32-07:00","id":1520108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1515586-victoria-era-wod?p=1519960#post1519960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, yes. I would indeed have loved to do that. It would have been thematically similar to H:tR, taking the idea of individuals thrust into a war they didn\u2019t understand without support or knowledge, but without the Solar Exalted Lite powers of the Imbued. It was probably back when I was working on London by Night, and thinking how this setting would work for Hunters.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds fun! The Hammer Horror's use of Peter Cushing as the vampire hunter and his bevy of family members, compatriots and proteges would make for a fun troupe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}